digraph {
	135 [label="RoatheRank1Convo2 begins.",color=orange];
		135 -> 136;
	136 [label="You do realize that your so-called \"Indifference\" isn't an actual \"god,\" yes?",shape=box,color=blue];
		136 -> 139;
		136 -> 138;
		136 -> 137;
	139 [label="He's close enough to one.",shape=box,color=red];
		139 -> 142;
	138 [label="And what makes you so sure?",shape=box,color=red];
		138 -> 141;
	137 [label="[End.]",shape=box,color=red];
		137 -> 140;
	142 [label="Everyone I speak to around this madhouse is entirely convinced that this \"Man in the Wall\" is some kind of literal and laughable god. An actual god. Even those two zealots seem to be entertaining the idea!",shape=box,color=blue];
		142 -> 144;
		142 -> 145;
		142 -> 146;
	141 [label="Well, setting aside the harsh reality that any belief in a god or gods comes from idiots who cling to: One, a crushing need to clutch a stuffed animal when one faces the brutal horror of the finality of one's soul when it reaches death,",shape=box,color=blue];
		141 -> 143;
	140 [label="Chat ends.",color=orange];
	144 [label="You don't think he's real?",shape=box,color=red];
		144 -> 148;
	145 [label="And if you don't think he's a god, what do you think he is?",shape=box,color=red];
		145 -> 149;
	146 [label="And you don't?",shape=box,color=red];
		146 -> 150;
	143 [label="Two, the anxiety one suffers when you realize there is no \"Greater Power\" out there laying out our lives in front of us and therefore we simply are responsible for our own actions and therefore, by extension,",shape=box,color=blue];
		143 -> 147;
	148 [label="Now, did I say those words? Do not be so quick to put words into my mouth, Oh Transient Usurper. I did not deny that the Indifference was \"real.\" I denied that it was a God.",shape=box,color=blue];
		148 -> 152;
		148 -> 153;
	149 [label="I can disrobe this false deity for you in two simple words you should know and understand quite well:",shape=box,color=blue];
		149 -> 154;
	150 [label="Absolutely not! First, there are no god or gods, the idea is absurd. Second, to think that Albrecht let loose a god of the Void? Even more laughable!",shape=box,color=blue];
		150 -> 155;
	147 [label="Three, the righteous anger that accompanies the anxiety and horror, when all this leads to the epiphany that there is no \"Hell\" waiting for Devils, nor any \"Heaven\" waiting for Angels.",shape=box,color=blue];
		147 -> 151;
	152 [label="That thing is more powerful than anything I've ever been up against.",shape=box,color=red];
		152 -> 156;
	153 [label="What do you think he is, then?",shape=box,color=red];
		153 -> 149;
	154 [label="Conceptual Embodiment.",shape=box,color=blue];
		154 -> 157;
		154 -> 158;
		154 -> 159;
	155 [label="There is nothing in the Void. That is why it is named the Void! ",shape=box,color=blue];
		155 -> 160;
		155 -> 161;
	151 [label="I am assuming you are not an drooling zealot who clings to anger, horror, or anxiety. Operating on this assumption, I am going to move forward with the second argument I wish to present to you for the disrobement of \"the Indifference's\" Godhood:",shape=box,color=blue];
		151 -> 154;
	156 [label="And when have I denied that, either? Indeed, it seems you have all managed to spin yourselves into quite a hysterical and needlessly egregious bit of tribulation.",shape=box,color=blue];
		156 -> 162;
		156 -> 163;
	157 [label="The Void and what we can make of it is dangerous and powerful - trust me, I know. But it has limits. You really think it's capable of manifesting something like that? That can create whole languages, fingers that can power ships that jump through the Void?",shape=box,color=red];
		157 -> 164;
	158 [label="It's... very tempting to believe that it's just a monster under our bed, Roathe. But I've seen this thing, face to \"face,\" and I don't know how something like that just comes out of our minds.",shape=box,color=red];
		158 -> 165;
	159 [label="Conceptual Embodiment cannot do what the Man in the Wall is capable of doing. While Entrati may have manifested that thing - and is responsible for bringing it here - I don't believe he is the original source of it.",shape=box,color=red];
		159 -> 166;
	160 [label="No. I've seen things that come from the Void. Angels. Singing. Ghosts.",shape=box,color=red];
		160 -> 167;
	161 [label="I... ",shape=box,color=red];
		161 -> 167;
	162 [label="What're you saying?",shape=box,color=red];
		162 -> 168;
	163 [label="Wait. How are we to blame for this? Albrecht is the one to blame, he set it loose.",shape=box,color=red];
		163 -> 169;
	164 [label="Humanity is certainly nothing if not creative in the breadth and magnitude of new forms of suffering it can concoct for itself, is it not? You yourself have been witness to many a form of cruelty I am sure no one could scare imagine was possible in the time of our dear zealots.",shape=box,color=blue];
		164 -> 170;
	165 [label="Ah, you are so close to the truth and yet so quick to dismiss it. You think it is \"tempting\" to believe it is a creation of your own mind as it would be easier to dismiss it if it were so? No, I think it makes it far more dangerous to face a creation of our own making than a god.",shape=box,color=blue];
		165 -> 171;
	166 [label="While I appreciate your humility, I challenge your limited understanding of the capability of human creativity - especially in regards to how it can devise new forms of suffering. Are you not in fact single-handedly responsible for conjuring your own universe from whole cloth?",shape=box,color=blue];
		166 -> 172;
	167 [label="The only thing that comes from the Void is that which we place within it - and what returns from it. It changes matter and energy - but it cannot create it.",shape=box,color=blue];
		167 -> 173;
	168 [label="What I am saying is this: Albrecht might have been the one who originally saw his own hubris staring back at him as the face of a grinning god of destruction, yes.",shape=box,color=blue];
		168 -> 174;
	169 [label="Albrecht might have been the one who originally saw his own hubris staring back at him as the face of a grinning god of destruction, yes.",shape=box,color=blue];
		169 -> 174;
	170 [label="+15 Chemistry",color=orange];
		170 -> 175;
	171 [label="An external foe can be understood. Manipulated. Defeated. Or perhaps even negotiated with, if it comes to that. They have weaknesses that can be exploited. But an internal foe? One of our own making? That is far more insidious indeed.",shape=box,color=blue];
		171 -> 176;
	172 [label="You yourself have been witness to many a form of cruelty I am sure no one could scare imagine was possible in the time of our dear zealots. ",shape=box,color=blue];
		172 -> 177;
	173 [label="Think, Drifter. These \"Void Angels\" of which you speak. These ghosts. Were they made of those already lost to the Void?",shape=box,color=blue];
		173 -> 178;
	174 [label="But you are all as equally to blame for continuing to roll this juba bug turd downhill for as long as you have, getting bigger with every scrap of feces it collects along the way!",shape=box,color=blue];
		174 -> 179;
	175 [label="As a species, we are quite wondrous in our ability to feed our fears new ways to destroy ourselves.",shape=box,color=blue];
		175 -> 180;
	176 [label="+20 Chemistry",color=orange];
		176 -> 181;
	177 [label="+10 Chemistry",color=orange];
		177 -> 175;
	178 [label="They were merely echoes of energy being regurgitated like a colorful kutak to feed its children.",shape=box,color=blue];
		178 -> 179;
	179 [label="Allow me to simplify the discussion for you. I can disrobe this false deity for you in two simple words you should know and understand quite well:",shape=box,color=blue];
		179 -> 154;
	180 [label="Mm. I fear I must go. I will let you sit with this for a time and ponder my words.",shape=box,color=blue];
		180 -> 182;
		180 -> 183;
	181 [label="Because then we must fight our own demons. And humanity... never wins such wars, do we?",shape=box,color=blue];
		181 -> 180;
	182 [label="I'll do that. Thanks.",shape=box,color=red];
		182 -> 184;
	183 [label="Ponder mine, you may end up wanting to believe them when you're up against an anti-god.",shape=box,color=red];
		183 -> 184;
	184 [label="Update boolean RoatheMITW1",color=orange];
		184 -> 185;
	185 [label="Chat ends.",color=orange];
}